From 8114ed60193760ec4e5dc5b07ac08c7095e07e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:40:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo: route SPK1
 OUT to the WSA8815

The speaker was silent on Debian with the v7.3 kernel. Without a route into
"SpkrLeft IN", the amplifier's DAPM path (IN -> RDAC -> SPKR PGA -> SPKR) has
an unconnected input. DAPM therefore powers it once, when the card binds,
whether or not anything plays.

The machine driver is a module, so the card binds about 7 s after the amp
probed. By then the amp is runtime-suspended and its regmap is cache-only.
The Bandgap (0x3103, volatile) and RDAC (0x311c, not cached yet) writes
fail with -EBUSY ("ASoC error (-16)" at boot). DAPM still marks both widgets
on and never writes them again, so SPKR_DAC_CTL stays at 0x42 (DAC off)
during playback. The linuxduobench 6.19 boot happened to bind the card
while the amp was awake: 0x311c = 0xc2 there.

Route SPK1 OUT to SpkrLeft IN, as db845c does. The amp's path then powers
with the playback stream, after ASoC has resumed the amp for the open
backend.
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi     | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
index 7c17d79ed..64722493e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
@@ -8,8 +8,16 @@
 &{/sound} {
 	/* Microsoft's DT (dtbo DV_A): DMIC1 is powered by MIC BIAS1, DMIC2 by MIC BIAS3 (mainline had no routing: the
 	 * DMICs stayed unpowered -> digital silence, rms 0) */
+	/*
+	 * SPK1 OUT (RX INT7) feeds the WSA8815, as on db845c. Without this route the amp's IN -> RDAC -> SPKR PGA -> SPKR
+	 * path has an unconnected input and DAPM powers it once, when the card binds. On a late card bind (the machine
+	 * driver is a module) the amp is already runtime-suspended then (regmap cache-only): the Bandgap (0x3103) and
+	 * RDAC (0x311c) writes fail with -EBUSY, DAPM still marks them on and never writes them again -> silent speaker.
+	 * With the route the path powers with the stream, after ASoC has resumed the amp.
+	 */
 	audio-routing = "DMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
-			"DMIC2", "MIC BIAS3";
+			"DMIC2", "MIC BIAS3",
+			"SpkrLeft IN", "SPK1 OUT";
 
 		/* a second front end (pcm 1,1) so capture and playback can run at once (one ASM session per FE:
 		 * "Audio Client already active" when both used MultiMedia1) - the speaker->mic loopback test */
-- 
2.43.0

